{
  "requirement": "The harness instructs the model to finish by calling\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission.mcp`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission` has one obligation: the harness instructs the model to finish by calling `submit_result`. The tool's shape and schema belong to `submission.mcp`, which is cited here as context. The acceptance rules belong to `submission.acceptance`. This assessment doesn't cover those.\n\nThe instruction is built in one place, `tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]`. That is a single code path, not several conditional ones.\n\nThree tests assert that the prompt delivered to the provider contains \"Finish by calling submit_result\":\n- `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` checks the serialized OpenAI request `input` on all four requests. That covers both the first turn and the follow-up turns after a tool result.\n- `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat]` checks the Ollama `messages` on both turns.\n- `tests.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` checks the first request's `chat_history` on the default provider path.\n\nEach of these tests carries a `{test}` reference to the subject, as do two more in `tests.rs`. `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` and `typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors` support the cited `submission.mcp` side. They check the `submit_result` tool's name, its `result` schema and that bad results become agent errors.\n\nIf the harness dropped or reworded the instruction, these assertions would fail. They run against the real wire formats and against the abstract provider. Nothing in the text requires further input classes or modes beyond these.",
  "references": "6d3090f0bb60675c1ce9da3313f3f3f65297e0a05452744687240cd1bb853491",
